    "result_text": "The build is green. Let me summarize what I changed.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the identity key and duplicate detection to match the new specification. The test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests green).\n\n### Changes\n\n**`Owner.java`** \u2014 `getIdentityKey()` now returns the full lower-case hex **SHA-256** over `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` (previously a plain concatenation of `telephone|email|householdId`). Added a self-contained, deterministic **American Soundex** implementation (`Owner.soundex(String)` plus a private digit-mapping helper) so both the key and the soft-match use one source of truth.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- The single hard-duplicate 409 check already keyed off `getIdentityKey()`, so it now uses the new SHA-256 key automatically \u2014 still skipping owners flagged deleted, and still running *after* `normalizeEmail` applies the disposable-domain blocklist. Because telephone is part of the key, two owners with the same last name and postcode but **different telephones** no longer collide \u2192 no 409.\n- `possibleDuplicateOf(...)` (the soft-match) now triggers when `soundex(lastName)` **and** postcode match but the whole `identityKey` **differs** (previously: exact last name + postcode + different telephone). Deterministic smallest-id tie-break retained.\n- Updated the explanatory comments; the `householdId`-based key is gone, and there was no longer a separate household-duplicate 409 block to remove.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `identityKey` field description and example to reflect the 64-hex SHA-256 form.\n\nThe exact soundex output isn't asserted by the tests (their oracle is \"identical identity \u2192 409\" plus the 64-hex shape), and the same `Owner.soundex` is used for both the key and the soft-match, so the two stay consistent.",
